course: dictionary
lesson: 6704
title: Words for strange things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An oddity is something strange or unusual. It can be a person, a thing or an event. In «The forest is full of oddities», the word means the forest has many strange and unusual things in it.
explain: Oddity has a second meaning too: being strange or unusual. This meaning cannot be counted, so it has no plural. Look for clues around the word, such as strange, unusual or a bit odd, to tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Context helps again. In «a monkey with a nose like a dangling cucumber», the words after the colon show which oddities the writer means. A colon often introduces examples, so the words after it explain the word before it.
fact: An oddity is a strange or unusual person, thing or event.
fact: Oddity can also mean being strange or unusual. This second meaning cannot be counted.
fact: «The forest is full of oddities» means the forest has many strange and unusual things in it.
fact: Phrases you may hear are "a bit of an oddity" and "an oddity of nature".
fact: Nature has oddities, such as the platypus, a mammal that lays eggs.
exercise: What does oddity mean? | A loud noise at night | *A strange or unusual person, thing or event | A plain, ordinary thing | A rule that everyone must follow
exercise: «The forest is full of oddities: a monkey with a nose like a dangling cucumber.» Find and copy one word that means strange things. | forest | cucumber | *oddities | monkey
exercise: Why is the platypus called an oddity of nature? | It is made of metal | It can fly like a bird | It lives in a big city | *It is a mammal that lays eggs
test: Tom says, "The oddity of the dark, empty house made him shiver." What does oddity mean here? | A loud sound | A happy memory | *Being strange and unusual | A small room
test: Which word fits best in the phrase "a bit of an ___"? | *oddity | gleam | castle | whisper
exam: Lily says the monkey with the cucumber nose is an oddity. Why? | It is a very small insect | It is a plant that grows in the ground | *It is a strange, unusual animal | It is a kind of heavy rain
